<section class="section"><div class="container article-body">
<h2>Buster Bar — What's Inside</h2>
<p>The Buster Bar has a more complex interior than the Dilly Bar. Inside the chocolate coating, you find DQ vanilla soft serve that has been layered with salted peanuts and fudge. The peanuts add crunch and saltiness; the fudge adds warm chocolate flavor. The combination of soft serve, peanuts, and fudge inside a chocolate shell is similar to the Peanut Buster Parfait experience, but in a portable stick format. Find all DQ classic treats on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>
<h2>Buster Bar vs. Dilly Bar — The Key Difference</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Price</th><th>Calories</th><th>What's Inside</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Buster Bar® Treat</td><td class="price-cell">$2.49</td><td>440 cal</td><td>Soft serve + peanuts + fudge + choc shell</td></tr><tr><td>Dilly® Bar (Chocolate)</td><td class="price-cell">$1.99</td><td>210 cal</td><td>Plain soft serve + chocolate shell</td></tr><tr><td>Non-Dairy Dilly® Bar</td><td class="price-cell">$2.49</td><td>220 cal</td><td>Dairy-free base + chocolatey coating</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2>Does the Buster Bar Contain Peanuts?</h2>
<p>Yes. The Buster Bar contains salted peanuts as a core ingredient. It is not suitable for guests with peanut allergies. For a peanut-free novelty treat, the Dilly Bar ($1.99) or Non-Dairy Dilly Bar ($2.49) are the right alternatives.</p>
