  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>The Buster Bar — DQ's Original Frozen Bar</h2>
    <p>The Buster Bar® Treat predates the Blizzard by decades. It is one of the original DQ novelty bars — vanilla soft serve layered with peanuts and fudge on a stick, coated in a chocolate shell. At $2.49 and 440 calories, it delivers considerably more flavor and substance than a <a href="/items/dilly-bar">standard Dilly Bar</a> for the same price. For all DQ treat options, visit <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>Buster Bar vs. Dilly Bar — Which to Choose?</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th></th><th>Buster Bar</th><th>Dilly Bar (Chocolate)</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Price</td><td class="price-cell">$2.49</td><td class="price-cell">$1.99</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Calories</td><td>440 cal</td><td>210 cal</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Contents</td><td>Soft serve + peanuts + fudge + chocolate shell</td><td>Soft serve + chocolate shell only</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Flavor</td><td>Rich, salty-sweet, multi-layered</td><td>Clean, simple, classic</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Best For</td><td>Guests who want more complexity and substance</td><td>Guests who want a simple, light novelty bar</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2>What's in the Buster Bar</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>DQ vanilla soft serve core</strong> — The same base used across all DQ frozen treats</li>
      <li><strong>Salted peanuts</strong> — Distributed throughout the soft serve for crunch and salt</li>
      <li><strong>Fudge layer</strong> — Chocolate fudge threaded through the soft serve</li>
      <li><strong>Chocolate shell coating</strong> — Hardens on contact with the cold soft serve, shatters on the first bite</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The Salty-Sweet Formula</h2>
    <p>The Buster Bar uses the same salty-sweet formula that makes the <a href="/items/peanut-buster-parfait">Peanut Buster Parfait</a> so enduringly popular — peanuts and fudge together. The difference is format: the Parfait is served in a cup with layered toppings, making it a sit-down treat. The Buster Bar is handheld, portable, and at $2.49 is $2.50 cheaper than the Parfait.</p>

    <h2>Best for Peanut Lovers</h2>
    <p>If you enjoy the <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese's Blizzard</a> or the <a href="/items/peanut-buster-parfait">Peanut Buster Parfait</a>, the Buster Bar is in the same flavor family — peanut, chocolate, and DQ soft serve — at the most portable and affordable format on the menu.</p>

